ve eased 10-year Treasury yields to the 4.65% area as of early August 2026, reflecting tempered growth expectations and reduced odds of near-term Fed rate hikes. With the federal funds target range at 3.50-3.75%, persistent inflation readings and elevated energy prices continue to anchor market-implied policy paths toward steady or modestly higher rates through year-end, limiting aggressive downside moves in longer-term yields. Treasury supply dynamics and investor demand for duration also influence the curve, while upcoming FOMC communications, CPI releases, and labor reports will serve as key catalysts that could shift trader consensus on how far yields compress before 2027 resolution.","context_requires_regen":true,"context_updated_at":"2026-08-08T05:16:35.656Z"},"version":"v1"}]
